From d41ebf42257b5f2a6662430896eb989e0f135fed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:48:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: remove SM8750 ISP register debug interface

The TFE pixel pipeline programs its defaults and image controls in the
driver. No product component uses the separate register scripts or live
register access.

Drop the unbounded MMIO interface and its single global CSID/VFE pointers,
which do not represent simultaneous front and rear streams. Keep the media
graph, controls, frame tracepoints and DMA error handling unchanged.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Makefile    |   1 -
 .../platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-980.c      |   5 -
 .../platform/qcom/camss/camss-isp-debug.c     | 215 ------------------
 .../platform/qcom/camss/camss-isp-debug.h     |  23 --
 .../platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen4.c      |   5 -
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c     |   7 -
 6 files changed, 256 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-isp-debug.c
 delete mode 100644 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-isp-debug.h

